---
description: End-to-end flow when Morris logs a hotel stay or stop-by (Travel > Hotel Collection)
alwaysApply: true
---

# New hotel visit

When Morris names a hotel, finish the visit in this order. Do not stop after JSON.

1. **Catalog name** — Find the hotel in `components/travel/data/hotels.json` (grep by city or brand) and use its `id` as `hotelId`. Card title, brand, family, city, and map pin all come from that row plus visit `type`. Not in the catalog → add a catalog row first (`id`, `name`, `brand`, `family`, `city`, `country`, `lat`, `lng`; brand/family pairs: Waldorf Astoria / Conrad / NoMad → Hilton Honors, The Ritz-Carlton / St. Regis / EDITION / W Hotels / JW Marriott → Marriott Bonvoy, Four Seasons → Four Seasons, Fairmont → ALL Accor). Never log a visit to an uncatalogued hotel.

2. **Type + dates** — `stay` = slept there (`date` is check-in, `checkout` is the morning he left; nights render as `checkout − date`). `stop-by` = drink, meal, or a look; no `checkout`. If Morris did not say which, or gave no date, **ask** — do not default silently (the renderer treats a missing `type` as `stay`, so a guess ships as a stay). Map pin is automatic from `type` + catalog `brand`: stay uses `components/travel/img/brands/<slug>-stay.png` (colored official emblem only, no wordmark; Fairmont stay is the original F on gold `#C5A35A`); stop-by uses the original black-and-white `components/travel/img/brands/<slug>.png`. If a brand has no official color emblem, both files use the black-and-white official mark until Morris supplies color art. Slugs: `waldorf-astoria`, `conrad`, `nomad`, `ritz-carlton`, `st-regis`, `edition`, `w-hotels`, `jw-marriott`, `four-seasons`, `fairmont`. Do not put pin fields on the visit JSON. A new catalog brand also needs both icon files before any visit can pin.

3. **Id** — `kebab-name-MMDDYY` from the hotel's short name + `date` (check-in). Repeat visits get a new id. Example: `the-roosevelt-new-orleans-011926`.

4. **JSON** — Append to `components/travel/data/hotel-visits.json`. `pictures` starts `[]`.

```json
{
  "id": "kebab-name-MMDDYY",
  "hotelId": "<catalog id from hotels.json>",
  "type": "stay",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "checkout": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "pictures": []
}
```

`type` is `stay` | `stop-by`. `checkout` is stay-only; omit it for a stop-by.

5. **Photos** — `mkdir -p components/travel/img/visits/<id>/`. Local agent: `open components/travel/img/visits/<id>/` (macOS) so Morris can drop files; a cloud agent cannot open Finder, so tell him the path. **Stop until he drops files.** Keep `0.jpeg` (cover, Morris names it). Rename the rest `1.jpeg`, `2.jpeg`, … sorted A–Z by **original** filename, then write `pictures`. Run `npm run compress-travel -- <id>` (same encode as dining: display max 2000px q85, `N.thumb.jpeg` max 640px q72). Passing `<id>` avoids re-encoding other visits. Every listed file needs `N.jpeg` + `N.thumb.jpeg`. Cards read decrypted blob URLs after unlock — do not point them at a public `img/travel/visits/` path.

6. **Encrypt** — Hotel Collection is a gated tab. After JSON + photos are ready: `GATE_DEVOTION_PASSWORD=... GATE_HOTELS_PASSWORD=... npm run gate-encrypt`. The passphrases come from Morris / the environment, never from git. This rewrites `components/gated/hotel-collection.enc` and `components/gated/hotel-media.enc`.

7. **Ship** — Commit the updated `components/gated/*` envelopes only, not plaintext JSON or visit photos: `backend(travel): add <Hotel short name> <stay|stop-by>` (e.g. `backend(travel): add Roosevelt New Orleans stay`). Tab UI changes are `frontend(travel):`. Push. If the working copy is missing plaintext catalog/visits, restore them first with `npm run gate-decrypt`.

## Do not

- Copy `name`, `brand`, `family`, `city`, `country`, `lat`, `lng` onto the visit — they live in the catalog only.
- Invent a catalog row's coordinates or brand; look them up.
- Invent or replace brand pin art when logging a visit — the stay/stop-by pairs already exist for every listed brand.
- Default `type` or `date` when Morris left them out.
- Add `checkout` to a `stop-by`, or omit it from a `stay`.
- Commit camera originals, or a visit whose `pictures` lack a `N.thumb.jpeg`.
- Commit plaintext `hotels.json`, `hotel-visits.json`, or `img/visits/` — those are gitignored. Only `components/gated/*` is public.
- Re-compress other visits or touch `components/dining/`.
